One evening, Lira found a shard beneath the kiln: a fragment of a mirror that reflected not faces, but possibilities. When she pressed the shard to her forehead, the room bloomed with visions of other kitchens, other families, other meals shared in warmth. The shard spoke without voice, a whisper threaded through the hiss of the kiln: "Shape not the world as you wish it, but as you believe it can be."

